+  | nemotron-3-super-120b | 6,687,190 | $1.02 | $1.02 |
+  | claude-sonnet-5-runtime | — | **$3.14** | $3.14 (unchanged — its cache rates are published and real) |
+
+  **Kimi is more expensive than Sonnet, not cheaper.** Every earlier figure in
+  this file applied Anthropic's 0.10× cache-read multiplier to arms that have no
+  such rate — the precise thing the pricing item above says must never be done
+  ("a gap in it must be reported, never estimated"). The cached fraction remains
+  worth *recording* — it is exogenous noise correlated with turn count, and a
+  reader needs to see it — but it must not move a dollar figure.
+
+  **Still open**, which is why this stays `[ ]`: the price book produces the
+  uncached figure as of 2026-08-23, but the figures *already written* do not.
+  Records collected before that carry `cost_usd: null` with `pricing_error` set
+  wherever a candidate returned a cache token — the log is append-only, so those
+  have to be re-priced in the derived view, keyed off `Versions.pricing_basis`,
