+
+- [ ] **`cache_state.warm` makes a Bedrock claim on a lottery arm.**
+  `_cache_warm` in `runner.py` reads turn-1 `cache_read` and stamps `True`/`False`
+  on every arm alike. On the candidates that is a claim about a product they do
+  not have: their `cache_read` is the serving layer's own per-worker KV reuse,
+  which is a lottery and not a Bedrock prompt-cache hit, so `False` there says
+  "this run was cold" about a cache that does not exist. Stored today: 14 gemma
+  records and 18 kimi records carry `cache_read > 0` with `warm: False`, which is
+  the same field answering two different questions in one column. Proposed fix: a
+  per-model gate returning `None` — undetermined, the fourth way to get there —
+  for any arm with no cache product, so only Sonnet's `warm` is a claim. Needs a
+  `SCHEMA_VERSION` bump: the *meaning* of an existing `False` changes on those
+  arms, which is exactly the case the version exists to keep readable.
